          "source_quote": "Λέγω αὐτῷ· Κύριε, ἄκουσόν μου ὀλίγων ῥημάτων.",
          "english_quote": "The opening listen and the request to be strengthened reflect edition choices reported by the 1891 apparatus against damaged/differing Athos wording.",
          "issue": "The note identifies affected wording but does not distinguish an editorial supplement or restoration from preserved text or a competing reading. Nor does it state the reported Athos alternatives. Consequently, readers cannot determine what kind of editorial choice is being disclosed. The supplied normalized Greek alone cannot establish these apparatus details.",
          "suggested_revision": "Provide the relevant apparatus transcription or a precise, attributed account identifying the status of both affected expressions and the reported alternatives. Explicitly distinguish any editorial supplement from preserved wording. Retain the selected working Greek in the translation; do not replace it merely because an alternative exists.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "edition": "simplified",
      "verdict": "revise",
      "checks": {
        "complete_coverage": false,
        "no_added_claims": true,
        "names_and_negations": true,
        "speaker_attribution": true,
        "source_choices_and_notes": false,
        "terminology_policy": true
      },
      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "καὶ ἔχων τόπον εἰσπορεύεται εἰς αὐτούς, καὶ ὃ δὲ βούλεται ἐν αὐτοῖς ἐργάζεται",
          "english_quote": "He has room to enter them and does whatever he wishes in them.",
          "issue": "The Greek separately asserts that the devil has room, enters them, and acts in them. The simplified text expresses room or opportunity to enter but omits the actual entry. His subsequent activity does not explicitly preserve that assertion.",
          "suggested_revision": "Proposed correction for fresh review: “Having room, he enters them and does whatever he wishes in them.”",
          "severity": "major"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "Λέγω αὐτῷ· Κύριε, ἄκουσόν μου ὀλίγων ῥημάτων.",
          "english_quote": "The opening listen and the request to be strengthened reflect edition choices reported by the 1891 apparatus against damaged/differing Athos wording.",
          "issue": "The simplified edition independently inherits an incomplete source-choice disclosure: the note does not identify whether the affected wording is preserved, supplied editorially, or selected against another reading, and it does not state the reported Athos alternatives. Those distinctions cannot be recovered from the supplied normalized Greek.",
          "suggested_revision": "Supply the relevant apparatus evidence or a precise, attributed account of the alternatives and editorial status of both expressions. Clearly label any supplementation while retaining the disclosed working reading in the main text.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Both editions need revision. The standard translation covers the selected Greek clauses faithfully, but its apparatus note needs a clearer distinction between preserved text, editorial supplementation, and reported alternatives. The simplified translation additionally omits the explicit assertion that the devil enters the empty ones. Both preserve the difficult empty-jar comparison, the universal request for strengthening, the negations and conditional resistance, and policy-compliant servant terminology. This review evaluates the supplied working text and disclosures; it does not authenticate unseen apparatuses, editions, or manuscripts. Proposed wording remains subject to fresh review."
